我能向所有还记得电视上这个强大阵容的人致敬吗？

00:08:01.939 --> 00:08:02.779
You wouldn't miss a moment.
你不会错过任何一刻。

00:08:02.779 --> 00:08:04.420
You wouldn't miss one second of that.
你一秒钟都不会错过。

00:08:04.420 --> 00:08:06.259
That was three hours of TV.
那是整整三个小时的电视节目。

00:08:06.259 --> 00:08:11.139
actually, and I don't mention this very much, but on my sub stack, it's called dead father society.
说实话，我平时不怎么提起这个，但在我的Substack上，有一个栏目叫“死去的父亲协会”。

00:08:11.139 --> 00:08:12.958
My father passed away when I was 17.
我父亲在我17岁时去世了。

00:08:12.958 --> 00:08:15.939
I've just written a piece that's all about Thursday nights.
我刚写了一篇文章，全都是关于周四晚上的。

00:08:15.939 --> 00:08:18.006
It's all about what my dad and I would do.
全都是我和我爸爸以前会做什么。

00:08:18.006 --> 00:08:23.811
We would go for pizza and some other stuff, and then we would go home and we would watch those four, maybe five shows.
我们会去吃比萨饼和别的什么，然后回家看那四部，也许五部剧。

00:08:23.811 --> 00:08:24.311
Wow.
哇。

00:08:24.311 --> 00:08:26.870
So yeah, very, very meaningful night for me as well.
所以对我也一样，这是一个非常有意义的夜晚。

00:08:26.870 --> 00:08:27.370
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

00:08:27.370 --> 00:08:28.944
I can't wait to read that, Alec.
我迫不及待想读那篇文章，亚力克。

00:08:28.944 --> 00:08:30.223
Everyone should read that.
每个人都该读读。

00:08:30.223 --> 00:08:33.421
And that's, I mean, it's hard to explain to people what that was.
而且，我是说，很难向人们解释那意味着什么。

00:08:33.421 --> 00:08:34.208
We were in 2025.
我们现在身处2025年。

00:08:34.208 --> 00:08:39.620
There's There's kind of the lack of that shared experience, the lack of the campfire we're all sitting around.
那种共同的体验有些缺失了，那种大家围坐在一起的“篝火”不见了。

00:08:39.259 --> 00:08:40.259
I think that's...
我觉得那是……

00:08:40.259 --> 00:08:41.259
The mono culture.
单一文化。

00:08:41.259 --> 00:08:42.259
Yeah.
对。

00:08:42.259 --> 00:08:45.899
I think that's a huge problem, sociologically, we won't get into that right now.
我认为从社会学角度来看这是一个巨大的问题，我们现在就不展开聊了。

00:08:45.899 --> 00:08:47.340
But we had that, right?
但我们曾经拥有过，对吧？

00:08:47.340 --> 00:08:49.740
And Family Ties was really in the center of that family.
而《结蒂家情》真的是那个家庭的核心。

00:08:49.740 --> 00:08:55.860
I talk about how Cheers was one of the biggest influences on me as a writer, part of why I wanted to be a comedy writer.
我经常说《欢乐酒店》对我的编剧生涯产生了巨大影响，这也是我想成为一名喜剧编剧的部分原因。

00:08:55.860 --> 00:08:59.220
But I don't think I say it often enough that Family Ties was very much up in that conversation.
但我说得可能还不够多，那就是《结蒂家情》也绝对在那个讨论范围内。

00:08:59.220 --> 00:09:08.500
I know for Carter, too, who's also from Ohio, talk about a show that was hilarious and and it could also be very moving and complicated and really nuanced, yeah.
我也知道对卡特来说，他也是俄亥俄州人，说到一部既搞笑又能让人感动、情节复杂且极其细腻的剧，就是它了。

00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:11.059
Do you know why I know what SCUBA stands for?
你知道为什么我知道SCUBA（水肺）是什么意思吗？

00:09:11.059 --> 00:09:12.700
Self-contained underwater breathing apparatus.
自携式水下呼吸器。

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:14.779
Self-contained underwater breathing apparatus.
自携式水下呼吸器。

00:09:14.779 --> 00:09:16.779
Underwater breathing apparatus.
水下呼吸器。

00:09:16.779 --> 00:09:18.860
Mallory has a breakthrough study here on that.
马洛里在这方面有一项出色的研究。

00:09:18.860 --> 00:09:19.700
Yes, study for the great show.
是的，为了这个伟大的节目做研究。

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:21.860
She's not a great student, absolutely.
她绝对不是个好学生。

00:09:21.860 --> 00:09:22.700
Brilliant.
太精彩了。

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:24.259
And so talk about what that meant to you.
那么谈谈这对你意味着什么吧。

00:09:24.259 --> 00:09:26.259
It was set in literally where you're from, right?
它故事发生的背景可以说是你的家乡，对吧？

00:09:26.259 --> 00:09:27.419
Yeah, it's set in Columbus, Ohio.
对，背景设在俄亥俄州哥伦布市。

00:09:27.419 --> 00:09:31.299
What did that feel like when you're at that age and you're watching a TV show be set there?
当你处于那个年龄，看到一部电视剧把背景设在那里，是什么感觉？

00:09:31.299 --> 00:09:35.539
Like was that one of those moments said, set you on your path?
这算不算是那些指引你走上人生道路的时刻之一？

00:09:35.539 --> 00:09:42.539
Well, yeah, I mean, I watched, it's so funny, I'm not a big TV watcher now, but I was a big TV watcher when I was a kid.
嗯，对，我的意思是，我看过——说来也奇怪，我现在不怎么看电视，但我小时候是个电视迷。

00:09:42.539 --> 00:09:52.539
I really loved television and I loved sitcoms, I loved Alice, I, you know, I loved Taxi, I loved, I would watch Barney Miller when there was nothing else, you know?
我真的很喜欢电视，我喜欢情景喜剧，我喜欢《爱丽丝》，你知道的，我喜欢《出租车》，没事的时候我还会看《巴尼·米勒》，你知道吗？

00:09:52.539 --> 00:10:01.419
I watched a lot of TV and family ties was probably like pound for pound, my favorite show.
我看了很多电视，《天才家庭》可能是我最喜欢的节目，不相上下。

00:10:01.419 --> 00:10:03.659
like just moment to moment delight.
就像每一个瞬间都充满欢乐。

00:10:03.659 --> 00:10:10.139
And I think, you know, it was so perfectly cast, there was just such a light touch around it.
而且我认为，你知道，它的演员阵容太完美了，整部剧的处理手法非常轻松。

00:10:10.139 --> 00:10:14.299
It's hard to do a family show that is both moving, but not trickly, you know.
要做一部既感人又不做作的家庭剧是很难的，你知道的。

00:10:14.299 --> 00:10:18.179
It was a great idea, just for anyone listening who's a little bit younger may not have seen film made eyes.
这是一个很棒的想法，对于任何可能没看过《天才家庭》的年轻听众来说。

00:10:18.179 --> 00:10:19.820
First of all, go find it and stream it.
首先，去找来看看并在线播放吧。

00:10:19.820 --> 00:10:24.340
I, we don't make any money by plugging that show, but please, it's phenomenal.
我，我们宣传那个节目拿不到一分钱，但拜命大家去看看，它太棒了。

00:10:24.340 --> 00:10:28.299
But the premise is, it's these hippie parents, right?
但它的前提是，这是一对嬉皮士父母，对吧？

00:10:28.299 --> 00:10:35.899
That we're kind of coming of age in the 60s as these piece love of the front lines of all the marches and protests.
他们在60年代度过青春期，作为反战和平运动的亲历者，走在游行和抗议的最前线。

00:10:35.899 --> 00:10:44.059
Right, with wonderful politics, like the wonderfully humanistic politics, like they're just these menchy people and they have a family, they have three kids.
没错，有着极佳的政治立场，就像那种极具人情味的政治立场，他们就是这种正派的人，他们有一个家庭，有三个孩子。

00:10:44.059 --> 00:10:46.699
And one of them turns out to be Alex P.
其中一个竟然是亚历克斯·P·

00:10:46.699 --> 00:10:48.933
Keaton, which launched Michael J.
基顿，这个角色把迈克尔·J·

00:10:48.933 --> 00:10:52.859
Fox into the Stratospheric, who was a genius in that role.
福克斯推向了事业的巅峰，他在那个角色中简直是个天才。

00:10:52.860 --> 00:10:54.460
Genius, genius performance.
天才，绝佳的表演。

00:10:54.460 --> 00:11:01.779
And he is this young Republican in a suit, I think young Republican in a suit influenced Barney Stinson.
他是一个穿着西装的年轻共和党人，我觉得穿着西装的年轻共和党人影响了巴尼·斯廷森。

00:11:01.779 --> 00:11:03.779
Honestly, Carter and I would talk about that sometimes.
老实说，卡特有时会和我谈起这个。

00:11:03.779 --> 00:11:07.019
Like I think that's part, that is part of the influence.
我觉得这确实是部分影响所在。

00:11:07.019 --> 00:11:13.139
And so it's that idea of parents having a kid and the kid is a little bit of like an alien to them, right?
所以这体现了这样一种理念：父母生了一个孩子，而这个孩子对他们来说有点像个外星人，对吧？

00:11:13.139 --> 00:11:16.259
And there are these two sisters too who each have different personality quirks.
家里还有两个姐妹，每个人都有不同的性格怪癖。

00:11:16.259 --> 00:11:17.820
Like Mallory's not a great student.
就像马洛里学习不是很好。

00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:30.860
Alex is like a double A plus like overachiever, but with this like serious like Ronald Reagan, like obsession, it's just a great, It was a show that talked comedically about family dynamics and politics.
亚历克斯是个全A加的超级优等生，但对罗纳德·里根有一种严重般的痴迷，这真是一个伟大的节目，它以喜剧的方式探讨了家庭动态和政治。

00:11:30.860 --> 00:11:33.299
It's almost hard to imagine, right?
几乎很难想象，对吧？

00:11:33.299 --> 00:11:37.340
At this moment in 2025 that there could be this show that could just make that okay.
在2025年的当下，居然能有一部剧把这一切处理得如此自然。

00:11:37.340 --> 00:11:45.740
Beyond the political stuff, it was really an illustration of whatever you are and whatever you think you're handing off to your kids, they're probably gonna attack the other way.
抛开政治内容不谈，它真正说明了一点：无论你是谁，无论你认为自己传授给孩子什么观念，他们很可能会走向反方向。

00:11:45.740 --> 00:11:47.899
Like they're not gonna be carbon copy.
他们不会是你的复制品。

00:11:47.899 --> 00:11:49.139
They're their own people.
他们是独立的个体。

00:11:49.139 --> 00:11:50.340
They're their own people.
他们是独立的个体。

00:11:50.340 --> 00:11:51.899
And it was so brilliant at that.
这方面的表现真是太出色了。

00:11:51.899 --> 00:12:03.240
All of which is to say, this is a long way to say, The Father on that show was played by Michael Gross, who played Ted's Father.
所有这一切都是为了说明，兜了这么大一个圈子想说的是，剧中父亲的扮演者是迈克尔·格罗斯，也就是泰德父亲的扮演者。

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:13.240
And I wrote you this little day to send you in New York City.
我为你写了这段小日程，送你在纽约市使用。

00:12:13.240 --> 00:12:23.950
We'll be right back.
我们马上回来。

00:12:23.950 --> 00:12:26.070
And now, back to the show.
现在，回到节目中。

00:12:26.070 --> 00:12:32.149
Now I mentioned going back to yourself, Josh, trying traveling back to past you and saying, that guy's gonna play my dad on TV.
现在我提到回到过去的自己，乔治，试着回到过去的自己，然后对他说，那家伙以后要在电视里演我爸了。

00:12:32.149 --> 00:12:33.429
10, 11, 12, 13.
10、11、12、13。
10、11、12、13。

00:12:33.429 --> 00:12:39.190
However old I was when I'm watching these shows and it's my favorite show.
无论我看这些节目时我是几岁，它都是我最喜欢的节目。

00:12:39.190 --> 00:12:41.590
And then I grow up, I become a professional actor.
然后我长大了，成为了一名专业演员。

00:12:41.590 --> 00:12:43.591
I get on this big show and Alex P.
我参演了这部大热剧，而亚历克斯·P·

00:12:43.591 --> 00:12:47.830
Keaton's father, the guy who played his father is now playing my father.
基顿的父亲，也就是扮演他父亲的那个人，现在在演我的父亲。

00:12:47.830 --> 00:12:54.429
And I don't think Michael, like I don't know that I was able to communicate how important family ties was to me.
而且我觉得迈克尔——我不知道我是否能够表达清楚《天才家庭》对我的重要性。

00:12:54.429 --> 00:13:00.629
You know, he's obviously, he's a guest star on now my show, which was trippy and vertigo-inducing.
你知道，他显然现在是我的节目的客串明星，这感觉很不真实，让人目眩神迷。

00:13:00.629 --> 00:13:01.750
But definitely.
但绝对是这样的。

00:13:01.750 --> 00:13:10.110
But to me, he was just a face and a voice that was emblazoned onto my consciousness in the same way I'm sure I am for other people.
不过对当时的关我而言，他只是一个面孔和声音，深深烙印在我的意识里，就像我相信我也这样印在其他人心里一样。

00:13:10.110 --> 00:13:10.950
Yeah.
对啊。

00:13:10.950 --> 00:13:13.269
And did you attempt to tell him?
那你尝试告诉过他吗？

00:13:13.269 --> 00:13:14.909
Did you dork out on him a little bit?
你在他面前表现得很狂热、很迷弟吗？

00:13:14.909 --> 00:13:19.070
Or he was so down to earth, he didn't come in with any kind of ego about it.
还是说他非常脚踏实地，完全没有什么明星架子？

00:13:19.070 --> 00:13:19.909
No.
没有。

00:13:19.909 --> 00:13:21.990
And it'd been a minute since family ties, even then.
而且即使在那个时候，距离《成长的烦恼》播出也已经过去好一阵子了。

00:13:21.990 --> 00:13:25.029
But I was star struck by him for sure.
但我见了他确实感到非常崇拜和震撼。

00:13:25.029 --> 00:13:30.029
He still had an easy way about him, both often on screen.
无论在幕前还是幕后，他身上总是有一种随和放松的气质。

00:13:30.029 --> 00:13:33.379
He's an actor to me that doesn't push, you know.
对我来说，他是一个演戏从不流于表面的演员，你知道的。

00:13:33.379 --> 00:13:34.220
That's right.
没错。

00:13:34.220 --> 00:13:36.539
He underplays it, and it plays very real.
他处理得很克制，但演得非常真实。

00:13:36.539 --> 00:13:38.539
He's underplaying it, he's pretty relaxed.
他的表演很内敛，而且相当放松。

00:13:38.539 --> 00:13:47.779
He's, you know, and he seems like a dad who probably did some things well, and some things not so.
他给人的感觉就像是一个父亲，可能有些事情做得很好，有些事情则不那么完美。

00:13:47.779 --> 00:13:48.940
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

00:13:48.940 --> 00:14:03.379
He, it was just a delight to, I remember in the early seasons of Howie Mary Mother, that was the thing, for some reason, the fact that Michael Gross from Family Ties was playing my father on television, was the strangest thing of all of it.
他……能跟他合作简直是一种享受。我记得在《老爸老妈浪漫史》的前几季里，最不可思议的一点——不知为什么，因参演《成长的烦恼》而走红的迈克尔·格罗斯竟然在电视上扮演我的父亲，这成了整部剧里最奇妙的事情。

00:14:03.379 --> 00:14:07.580
I mean, I like the idea of younger you somehow knowing that someday.
我是说，我挺喜欢这种假设的：年轻时的你 irgendwie（不知怎么的）知道自己有一天会……

00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:11.379
Like I just, it's mind blowing if you could have somehow known that.
就好像，如果你当时能预知这一切，那真的太让人震撼了。

00:14:11.379 --> 00:14:16.460
Now, did you, it is an episode about not communicating in a family, right?
话说回来，这一集讲的是一个关于家庭缺乏沟通的故事，对吧？

00:14:16.460 --> 00:14:18.259
Our episode, I mean, all right, right?
我说的是我们这一集，没错吧？

00:14:18.259 --> 00:14:23.620
This is an episode where Ted's parents do not know how to talk to him and he does not know how to talk to them.
这一集讲的是泰德的父母不知道该怎么跟他说话，而他也不知道该怎么跟他们沟通。

00:14:23.620 --> 00:14:26.100
Did that resonate for you guys, in the writers?
这在你们编剧当中引起共鸣了吗？

00:14:26.100 --> 00:14:28.899
Well, I wanna say my parents sometimes listen to this show.
嗯，我想说我的父母有时会收听这个节目。

00:14:28.899 --> 00:14:30.860
So I just want to say I love them.
所以我只想说我爱他们。

00:14:30.860 --> 00:14:32.460
I love them very dearly.
我非常非常爱他们。

00:14:32.460 --> 00:14:45.379
You know, I don't think I had to dig very deep for like parents from Ohio and you kind of want to take them a little deeper and they're, you know, but, you know, it's, I think that that's a generational thing.
你知道，我觉得自己不需要为了塑造来自俄亥俄州的父母而去挖掘多深的体验，而且你多少会想让他们显得更立体一点，他们呢……但你知道，我觉得这是一种代际现象。

00:14:45.379 --> 00:14:47.860
Like I've talked about this with my father.
就像我跟我父亲聊过这个。

00:14:47.860 --> 00:14:50.980
Like I think my parents and I have different love languages.
我觉得我和我父母有不同的爱的表达方式。

00:14:50.980 --> 00:14:56.580
Like there's not a button that my mom will not sew onto a shirt for me.
比如说，我妈没有什么纽扣是不会帮我缝到衬衫上的。

00:14:56.580 --> 00:14:58.500
There's not a shirt she won't iron.
没有什么衬衫是她不肯熨的。

00:14:58.500 --> 00:15:04.019
there's not a creamer that I don't want that's not in the refrigerator or would I get home.
没有哪个我想要的咖啡伴侣是我一回家冰箱里没有的。

00:15:04.019 --> 00:15:10.259
My dad, I had this lawsuit on this patio that's gone on for years.
至于我爸，我为了这个露台的法律纠纷已经持续了好几年。

00:15:10.259 --> 00:15:18.500
It's thankfully my God coming to a close, but my dad gave me hundreds of hours of free legal advice and counsel on this thing.
谢天谢地，上帝保佑，这件事快要结束了，但为此我爸给了我几百个小时的免费法律建议和咨询。

00:15:18.500 --> 00:15:24.500
And if they see key lime pie on the menu, they'll pick it up and it'll be in the fridge when I get, you know what I mean?
而且如果他们看到菜单上有青柠派，他们就会买下来，等我回家时它就会静静躺在冰箱里，你知道我的意思吗？

00:15:24.500 --> 00:15:27.100
Like there's different ways to love and communicate.
这就是不同的爱和沟通方式。

00:15:27.100 --> 00:15:33.259
And I'm really into words of affirmation and deep communication, and sometimes that's been like a struggle or a navigation.
而我本人非常热衷于肯定的话语和深入的交流，有时候这确实是一种挣扎或需要摸索的过程。

00:15:33.259 --> 00:15:36.899
Like I always kind of want to lure them into more open communication.
比如我总是想引导他们进行更开放的沟通。

00:15:36.899 --> 00:15:40.899
So I don't think I had to dig that deep for this part of that, you know?
所以我认为，为了演好这一部分，我不需要挖掘得太深，你懂的？

00:15:40.899 --> 00:15:43.419
Yeah, well, the writer's room certainly didn't.
对啊，编剧室里的其他人当然也不需要。

00:15:43.419 --> 00:15:47.019
The writer's room definitely Carter's also from Ohio.
