And I can't explain why.
我也说不出为什么。

00:33:55.250 --> 00:33:56.250
What is that?
这是怎么回事？

00:33:56.250 --> 00:33:59.250
I know, I'm sure we talked about it at length and arrived at 83 as it's perfect.
我懂，我确信我们曾深入讨论过，最后得出结论：83%就是最完美的。

00:33:59.250 --> 00:34:02.650
It's like enough of like an almost be, it's like a BB mine.
它就像是一个差不多能达到的数字，就像是一颗气枪铅弹。

00:34:02.650 --> 00:34:08.130
Like it's like enough of what he's trying to prove that it's statistically probable.
它刚好达到了他试图证明的那种具有统计学可能性的程度。

00:34:08.130 --> 00:34:12.690
Any lower it wouldn't be convincing and any higher it's unrealistic.
再低一点就没有说服力了，再高一点就不切实际了。

00:34:12.690 --> 00:34:14.130
And he knows that intuitively.
而他凭直觉就知道这一点。

00:34:14.130 --> 00:34:14.969
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

00:34:14.969 --> 00:34:15.809
He feels that.
他能感觉到。

00:34:15.809 --> 00:34:16.650
He has to hit that number.
他必须击中这个数字。

00:34:16.650 --> 00:34:19.929
It's the universal number, it's Fitzpye, it's whatever the...
这是个通用的数字，它是……

00:34:19.929 --> 00:34:24.170
Ted was wearing a shirt that I wanted to say, what were we doing with that shirt?
泰德穿了一件衬衫，我很想说，我们穿那件衬衫到底在干什么？

00:34:24.170 --> 00:34:25.550
There was some weird shirts.
有些衬衫真的很诡异。

00:34:25.550 --> 00:34:29.829
I called it out, so I was watching it with my wife, and I said, what's going on with that shirt right there?
我把它指出来了，当时我和我妻子一起看，我说：那件衬衫到底是怎么回事？

00:34:29.829 --> 00:34:30.949
What's happening, Wyze?
这到底是要闹哪样，威兹（Wyze）？

00:34:30.949 --> 00:34:31.789
It's a crate, right?
是个板条箱，对吧？

00:34:31.789 --> 00:34:38.110
It had these crazy swirly designs, light colored, but with this red dragon kind of design.
上面有那种疯狂的漩涡图案，颜色很浅，但带着这种红龙一样的设计。

00:34:38.110 --> 00:34:42.829
Was it almost, it almost looked like suede or like, kind of cowboy-ish?
是不是有点像，几乎看起来像麂皮，或者有点像牛仔风格？

00:34:42.829 --> 00:34:44.110
Cowboy-ish, yes.
牛仔风格，是的。

00:34:44.110 --> 00:34:55.429
And also for some reason, and I don't know what, me and the costume designer at the time were deciding, but like, it was either, sometimes I'd wear the shirts open, but I don't understand why I didn't button them more.
而且出于某种原因，我也不知道为什么，当时我和服装设计师在决定，但就像，要么是，有时我会把衬衫敞开穿，但我真不明白为什么我当时不多扣几颗扣子。

00:34:55.429 --> 00:34:59.230
There was always, there were always like three or four buttons on it.
总是，上面总是有三四颗扣子。

00:34:59.230 --> 00:35:00.309
All of the buttons open.
所有的扣子都敞开着。

00:35:00.309 --> 00:35:01.989
All of it like, sometimes too.
有时全都是这样。

00:35:01.989 --> 00:35:02.829
Yeah.
是啊。

00:35:02.829 --> 00:35:04.510
All of the buttons open, I can make a sale for it still.
扣子全敞开，我到现在还能靠它卖出点什么呢。

00:35:04.510 --> 00:35:07.030
Okay, but you only want, when it's some of them, it's weird.
好吧，但你只想，当只是其中几颗的时候，这很奇怪。

00:35:07.030 --> 00:35:09.269
Some of them, they were just such a weird thing.
其中一些，它们实在是太奇怪了。

00:35:09.269 --> 00:35:10.110
That's all.
就这样。

00:35:10.110 --> 00:35:10.949
Yeah.
是啊。

00:35:10.949 --> 00:35:16.059
All I will say is this, I will say this, I called out that shirt and my wife watching with me, she goes, I like that shirt.
我只想说这个，我想说的是，我指出了那件衬衫，和我一起看的我妻子说，我喜欢那件衬衫。

00:35:16.059 --> 00:35:18.059
And I was gonna go on a whole tirade against the shirt.
而我本来打算对那件衬衫大加挞伐。

00:35:18.059 --> 00:35:21.260
And then she was like, I kind of like it's, I don't know, maybe works for something.
然后她说，我其实挺喜欢它的，我不知道，也许在某些方面还挺合适的。

00:35:21.260 --> 00:35:34.579
By the way, the internet points out many times that Ted and the color, I'm colorblind, I trust the internet, that the color of Ted and Robin shirts are the same as the color of Ted's parents' shirts.
顺便说一句，互联网多次指出，泰德和颜色——我是色盲，我相信互联网——泰德和罗宾衬衫的颜色和泰德父母衬衫的颜色是一样的。

00:35:34.579 --> 00:35:41.099
I thought that was intentional, although I forgot whether it was intentional for me, but from the cost environment.
我以为那是刻意安排的，虽然我忘了对我来说是不是刻意的，但从服装部门的角度来看。

00:35:41.099 --> 00:35:47.380
It's hard to say that shirt was like, ah, well, classic, it was just a period, the function of being 2006.
很难说那件衬衫就像是，啊，嗯，经典，那只是一个时代，2006年的产物。

00:35:47.380 --> 00:35:48.980
Was that a thing in 2006?
那是2006年的流行趋势吗？

00:35:48.980 --> 00:35:52.340
I thought there were a few shirts but I'm like, whatever, I don't know what was happening.
我以为有几件衬衫，但我想，随便吧，我不知道当时发生了什么。

00:35:52.340 --> 00:35:54.820
But I don't think it was, it wasn't the brunch shirt.
但我不认为那是，那不是早午餐衬衫。

00:35:54.820 --> 00:35:56.179
It was another shirt.
那是另一件衬衫。

00:35:56.179 --> 00:35:57.019
It was another one.
是另一件。

00:35:57.019 --> 00:35:58.860
It was when they step out in the hall with his dad.
那是他们和他父亲一起走到走廊里的时候。

00:35:58.860 --> 00:36:00.019
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
对，对，对。

00:36:00.019 --> 00:36:04.739
And it was, yeah, when you texted me that, I was like, I know exactly what Sherrod Josh is talking about.
而且是，是的，当你给我发那个信息时，我就想，我完全知道乔希说的是哪件衬衫。

00:36:04.739 --> 00:36:11.179
But you know what's funny, when they put you in these clothes, you, like sometimes they'll be like, no, no, no, no, it looks great.
但你知道有趣的是什么吗，当他们给你穿这些衣服时，你，就像有时候他们会说，不，不，不，不，这看起来好极了。

00:36:11.179 --> 00:36:12.179
You're like, really?
你就会想，真的吗？

00:36:12.179 --> 00:36:14.539
But you trust them, you know?
但你信任他们，你知道吗？

00:36:14.539 --> 00:36:17.780
And I, you know, I- How often did you veto?
而且我，你知道，我——你行使否决权的频率有多高？

00:36:17.780 --> 00:36:18.619
How often did you veto?
你行使否决权的频率有多高？

00:36:18.619 --> 00:36:20.179
You can veto.
你可以否决。

00:36:20.179 --> 00:36:26.179
but sometimes you'll have like a quick change and they'll be like, oh, this is just like a 30 second pop, right?
但有时你会有快速换装的时候，他们会说，哦，这只是一个30秒的镜头，对吧？

00:36:26.179 --> 00:36:32.980
I think I got more as the show went on, I got a little more, I would, I exercised my veto power and more.
我觉得随着剧集的播出，我越来越多了，我变得更多了一点，我会，我更多地行使了我的否决权。

00:36:32.980 --> 00:36:33.820
Yeah.
是啊。

00:36:33.820 --> 00:36:42.539
And I would say, I don't feel good in this or this, you know, but sometimes you just look back and some of those like cowboy shirts and some of those things, you're like, wow.
我会说，我穿这个或那个感觉不太好，你知道，但有时你回过头来看，其中一些牛仔衬衫和其中的一些东西，你会想，哇。

00:36:42.539 --> 00:36:44.460
There was a lot of cowboy shit going on.
当时有很多西部牛仔风的服装。

00:36:44.460 --> 00:36:46.579
Maybe was that a thing in 2006?
也许那是2006年的流行趋势？

00:36:46.579 --> 00:36:47.420
More than I thought it was?
比我想象的还要流行？

00:36:47.420 --> 00:36:48.579
That's the western, yeah.
那是西部风，对。

00:36:48.579 --> 00:36:50.380
It was a little Western thing.
有点西部风。

00:36:50.380 --> 00:36:51.219
I don't know.
我不知道。

00:36:51.219 --> 00:36:52.579
But why Ted, why is Ted wearing that?
但为什么是泰德，为什么泰德要穿那个？

00:36:52.579 --> 00:36:55.019
I don't, it was, it was odd in retrospect.
我不知道，现在回想起来，这很奇怪。

00:36:55.019 --> 00:36:56.699
And even in the moment, I was like, I don't know.
甚至在当时，我也在想，我不知道。

00:36:56.699 --> 00:37:00.860
I think Jason was a little more like, don't put me in stuff that I feel weird in.
我觉得杰森更倾向于：别让我穿让我觉得怪异的衣服。

00:37:00.860 --> 00:37:04.699
Like, I think I was a little more like, okay, even, I guess.
就像，我觉得我更倾向于：好吧，甚至，我猜。

00:37:05.780 --> 00:37:06.980
But who knows?
但谁知道呢？

00:37:06.980 --> 00:37:07.820
Right.
对。

00:37:07.820 --> 00:37:11.219
And I'm sure he felt great about the zip away pants for the calves.
而且我敢肯定，他对那条小腿处能拉链拆卸的裤子感觉棒极了。

00:37:11.219 --> 00:37:12.059
Well, also.
嗯，还有。

00:37:12.059 --> 00:37:12.900
He'd do it for comedy.
他这么做是为了搞笑。

00:37:12.900 --> 00:37:13.739
He would do it for God bless me.
他这么做是为了……天啊。

00:37:13.739 --> 00:37:14.940
He'd do it for comedic purposes.
他这么做纯粹是为了喜剧效果。

00:37:14.940 --> 00:37:16.940
Were there things that you liked Ted in?
泰德穿过的衣服里，有什么是你喜欢的吗？

00:37:16.940 --> 00:37:20.900
were there things where you would get in the wardrobe and you go, this is Ted Mosby.
有没有那么一些服装，你一穿上就会觉得：“这就是泰德·莫斯比。”

00:37:20.900 --> 00:37:24.980
I feel like this is the look, clearly this wasn't dead, what we're talking about.
我感觉这就是那种造型，显然这并不是指我们刚才说的死去的那些。

00:37:24.980 --> 00:37:31.420
A lot of it was, because you're in costume all day, essentially.
很多时候确实是这样，因为你基本上整天都穿着戏服。

00:37:31.420 --> 00:37:32.500
And a lot of them on the show.
而且剧里有很多套。

00:37:32.500 --> 00:37:36.260
Yeah, but you start actually wanting them more to dress like you, like you.
对，但你后来其实更希望他们穿得像你，就像你本人一样。

00:37:36.260 --> 00:37:37.099
Right.
对。

00:37:37.099 --> 00:37:38.900
Like I do wear a lot of plaid shirts.
就像我平时穿很多格子衬衫。

00:37:38.900 --> 00:37:40.300
I do wear a lot of T-shirts.
我穿很多T恤。

00:37:40.300 --> 00:37:41.300
I do wear jeans.
我穿牛仔裤。

00:37:41.300 --> 00:37:42.940
I do wear whatever.
我随便穿什么。

00:37:42.940 --> 00:37:44.579
I do wear justice khakis, no.
我穿正义卡其裤，才怪。

00:37:44.579 --> 00:37:53.000
But I think you start just wanting to be comfortable.
但我觉得你开始只是想要穿得舒服。

00:37:53.000 --> 00:37:57.739
Yeah, because it's all day long for hours and hours and hours and you're living on that set.
对，因为一穿就是整整一天，几个小时又几个小时，你就生活在那个片场里。

00:37:57.739 --> 00:38:01.380
I have certain like, golds and yellows kind of make my skin look weird.
我有一些比如金色和黄色之类的颜色，会让我的皮肤看起来很怪。

00:38:01.380 --> 00:38:12.440
So we always avoided, we mostly avoided those, you know, just things that you kind of know what your palette is, I guess, but mostly you end up, it's almost like you're going shopping.
所以我们总是避免，我们大多会避开那些颜色，你知道的，就是你大概知道自己适合什么色系，不过大部分时候到头来，感觉就像去购物一样。

00:38:12.440 --> 00:38:14.480
like you have a wardrobe fitting, right?
就像你要去试装对吧？

00:38:14.480 --> 00:38:20.760
And you go in there and they got a huge rack of clothes and you just burn through a lot of clothes and you just yes, no, they just yes, no it real quick.
你走进试衣间，那里有一大排衣服，然后你快速浏览很多衣服，马上就能定下要还是不要，非常快地做出决定。

00:38:20.760 --> 00:38:21.599
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

00:38:21.599 --> 00:38:28.639
And then sometimes they, I remember they didn't even, sometimes there'd be like, okay, you're only in one, that you're in the shirt the whole episode.
然后有时他们——我记得甚至有时会这样，比如：“好吧，你这场戏只有一套衣服，这一集里你都穿着这件衬衫。”

00:38:28.639 --> 00:38:31.039
So let's find one you really feel comfortable in.
所以让我们找一件你真正觉得舒服的。

00:38:31.039 --> 00:38:31.880
Yeah.
对。

00:38:31.880 --> 00:38:32.719
You know?
你知道吗？

00:38:32.719 --> 00:38:41.519
But largely you would, you would, whatever the yes was, you know, you're like a preschooler, like you go into your dressing room in the morning and it's laid out for you, you know?
但大部分时候，只要选定了，你就会像个学龄前儿童一样，早上走进化妆间，衣服都已经为你摆好了，你知道吧？

00:38:41.519 --> 00:38:42.519
It is really weird.
这真的很诡异。

00:38:42.519 --> 00:38:43.519
There is this.
确实有这种感觉。

00:38:43.519 --> 00:38:45.400
There is an infantilizing quality, right?
有一种将人婴儿化的特质，对吧？

00:38:45.400 --> 00:38:46.400
To be good.
好吧。

00:38:46.400 --> 00:38:47.400
Okay.
行。

00:38:47.400 --> 00:38:48.400
Now wear this.
现在穿这个。

00:38:48.400 --> 00:38:51.840
Someone that follows you to go to the bathroom to make sure you come back for you your lunch.
甚至有人跟着你去洗手间，确保你回来吃午饭。

