我发现自己和特德有很多相似之处，尤其是现在我和他刚开始时一样大，渴望结婚，拼命想找到所谓的“真爱”，坦白说，这些日子这似乎是一个不可能完成的任务。

00:54:50.610 --> 00:54:58.090
I also relate a lot to Robin, having gotten my bachelor's degree in journalism a couple years ago and still trying to find a way of getting my career started.
我也觉得我和罗宾很像，几年前我获得了新闻学学士学位，现在仍在努力寻找开启职业生涯的方法。

00:54:58.090 --> 00:55:00.969
but unfortunately, with not much luck on my side.
但遗憾的是，我的运气不太好。

00:55:00.969 --> 00:55:15.590
With every episode, whether it made me laugh, to forget just a little bit of what was going on in life, or whether it made me sad and showed me that others are going through the same struggles as I do, it provided me with hope that one day, maybe just one day, things will turn out better.
伴随着每一集，无论是让我开怀大笑、暂时忘却生活中的烦恼，还是让我难过并向我展示其他人也在经历与我一样的挣扎，它都给我带来了希望：总有一天，也许就有一天，情况会变得更好。

00:55:15.590 --> 00:55:30.989
The hope that I get from watching the show is also the hope I get from listening to this podcast, from how Josh, after doing many pilots with shows that didn't get picked up or got canceled later on, was finally able to be on a show that not only got picked up, it also became one of the best sitcoms of all time.
从看这部节目中获得的希望，也是我听这个播客时获得的希望。正如乔希在演了许多没有被选中或后来被取消的试播集后，终于能够出演一部不仅被选中、还成为史上最佳情景喜剧之一的节目。

00:55:30.989 --> 00:55:37.469
From how everything aligned for Craig and Carter and that Starbucks in order to bring this show to life and keep it going for nine seasons.
正如克雷格和卡特在星巴克里的一切契合，才让这部剧得以诞生并延续了九季。

00:55:37.469 --> 00:55:47.829
And so many countless stories like Courtney's, Coby's, Ashley's, and many others that are shared on the podcast that let me know that God's timing is perfect and one day I'll get my big break.
还有无数像考特尼、科比、阿什莉以及许多在播客中分享的其他人的故事，让我知道上帝的安排是完美的，总有一天我会迎来我的转机。

00:55:47.829 --> 00:55:50.309
With that said, I just wanna say thank you.
话虽如此，我只想说谢谢。

00:55:50.309 --> 00:56:01.248
Thank you for creating something that truly became the comfort show I needed at any point in my life and shows me no matter what I may be going through, there's always a reason for me to keep going.
谢谢你们创造了这样一部作品，它真正成为了我生活在任何阶段都需要的情感慰藉，并告诉我，无论我正在经历什么，我总有继续前行的理由。

00:56:01.248 --> 00:56:02.463
You guys are the best.
你们是最棒的。

00:56:02.463 --> 00:56:03.182
Thanks again.
再次感谢。

00:56:03.182 --> 00:56:04.949
Your friend from Utah, Jonathan.
来自犹他州的朋友，乔纳森。

00:56:06.570 --> 00:56:07.663
That's lovely.
太可爱了。

00:56:07.663 --> 00:56:09.459
There's a twist ending.
还有一个反转结尾。

