01:00:12.039 --> 01:00:38.039
Derry, here is the, here is the promise at the very beginning of this, if you remember back to the beginning of this podcast, okay, here are some clips, exclusive to you, the how we made your mother fans and the how I met your mother fans, never before heard audio book clips from my debut novel, that's somehow an app and of Josh Radner and Kobe smolders as two of the four characters of the book and here's a little taste of what they do in the audiobook.
黛里，这就是最初的承诺，如果你还记得这个播客刚开始的时候，好吧，这里有一些独家剪辑，专属于你们——《老爸老妈浪漫史》的粉丝们。这是我处女作有声书里从未公开过的音频片段，书名有点像个应用，由乔什·拉德纳和科比·史姆德斯饰演书中的四个角色中的两个，以下是他们在有声书中的精彩片段。

01:00:38.039 --> 01:00:48.906
The book comes out of this podcast episode is dropping the week of my publication date of the book which is November 4th Tuesday and I'm very very excited for the book and the audiobook also.
这本书的发布与本期播客节目的上线正值同一周，即11月4日周二，我对这本书以及有声书都感到非常非常兴奋。

01:00:48.906 --> 01:01:04.039
You should know that you're gonna hear Josh and Kobe reading in character as two of the four characters in this book so you'll hear Kobe introduce herself as the character of Paige, who is married to the character of Rob, who was voiced by Josh Radner, please enjoy.
你们应该知道，接下来会听到乔什和科比以剧中角色的身份进行朗读，他们是书中四个角色中的两个。你会听到科比自我介绍为佩姬（Paige）这个角色，她嫁给了罗布（Rob），罗布由乔什·拉德纳配音，请好好欣赏。

01:01:04.039 --> 01:01:09.730
Paige, Rob was now officially off on script.
佩姬，罗布现在正式脱离剧本开始创作了。

01:01:09.730 --> 01:01:11.690
And I was just off.
而我则完全脱节了。

01:01:11.690 --> 01:01:17.440
Sorry, when I get stressed, I start speaking like the narration on Sex and the City.
抱歉，当我感到压力大时，说话就会变得像《欲望都市》里的旁白一样。

01:01:17.440 --> 01:01:25.880
And so began the surreal, unholy process of my husband adapting my book, my life, into a screenplay.
于是，我那超现实的、荒谬的过程开始了——我丈夫把我的书、我的人生改编成剧本。

01:01:25.880 --> 01:01:32.338
would grab a coffee and say, have a good day, then walk down the hall to his office and close the door.
他会喝杯咖啡说声“祝你有美好的一天”，然后穿过走廊走进他的办公室，关上门。

01:01:32.338 --> 01:01:36.477
I swear I could hear the sound of knives being sharpened in there.
我发誓我能听到里面磨刀的声音。

01:01:36.477 --> 01:01:40.176
What was happening to my poor little book behind that door?
我那可怜的小书在那扇门后究竟遭遇了什么？

01:01:40.176 --> 01:01:41.681
What was being scrapped?
有什么内容被删掉了？

01:01:41.681 --> 01:01:47.450
At lunch, I'd see Rob in the kitchen and expect him to say something about how it was going.
午饭时，我会在厨房见到罗布，本以为他会说点进展如何之类的话。

01:01:47.450 --> 01:01:47.950
Nope.
并没有。

01:01:47.950 --> 01:01:53.656
He has a thing about not discussing works in progress, which is fine when it's not my book.
他有个原则，那就是不讨论尚未完成的作品——当这不是我的书时，这倒无所谓。

01:01:53.469 --> 01:01:59.489
It's like a surgeon stepping out of the OR and not telling you if your loved one survived the surgery.
这就像一个外科医生走出手术室，却不告诉你你的亲人是否挺过了手术。

01:01:59.489 --> 01:02:06.150
After lunch, Rob would head back into his office four hours, afraid to stop lest he lose the role he was on.
午饭后，罗布会回到他的办公室一待就是几个小时，生怕停下来就会打断他正好的灵感状态。

01:02:06.150 --> 01:02:10.110
I swear, the man did not get up to P when he wrote.
我发誓，这男人写作时连起身上个厕所都没有。

01:02:10.110 --> 01:02:15.960
I often wondered if he kept a creepy mason jar under his desk, but I was too scared to check.
我经常纳闷他是不是在桌子底下藏了个瘆人的梅森罐，但我又太害怕而不敢去检查。

01:02:15.960 --> 01:02:24.880
To be fair, if some other screenwriter, a stranger, had been hired instead of Rob, I I would've long since been cut out of the process entirely.
平心而论，如果换作别的编剧——一个陌生人被雇来代替罗布，那我早就被彻底排除在创作过程之外了。

01:02:24.880 --> 01:02:26.800
I kept reminding myself of this.
我不断地提醒自己这一点。

01:02:26.800 --> 01:02:30.599
Like a mantra, it's better that it's Rob.
就像念咒语一样：是罗布来写总归要好一些。

01:02:30.599 --> 01:02:32.429
But was it?
真的是这样吗？

01:02:32.429 --> 01:02:38.510
There were times staring down the hall at Rob's closed office door, hearing the clickety clack of his keyboard.
有时我盯着走廊那头罗布紧闭的办公室门，听着键盘的啪啪敲击声。

01:02:38.510 --> 01:02:40.110
Was that the delete key?
那是删除键的声音吗？

01:02:40.110 --> 01:02:41.869
Was he deleting?
他在删内容吗？

01:02:41.869 --> 01:02:46.789
When I wished it was literally anyone in the world, but him, some writer far away.
那时我多么希望门后坐的是世界上任何其他人，而不是他，哪怕是个远在天边的作家。

01:02:46.789 --> 01:02:49.429
Australia, Thailand, the North fucking pole.
澳大利亚、泰国、该死的北极。

01:02:49.429 --> 01:02:52.690
anywhere but down that long, echoing hallway.
去哪儿都行，只要不是在那条长长的、回音阵阵的走廊尽头。

01:02:52.690 --> 01:02:57.849
Even worse, news of the nascent film project had broken and now everyone was writing me.
更糟糕的是，这部电影项目初现雏形的消息已经走漏，现在所有人都在给我发信息。

01:02:57.849 --> 01:03:00.739
Congrats, are you psyched?
“恭喜啊，你兴奋吗？”

01:03:00.739 --> 01:03:04.969
Some days, I was sure I could hear my book screaming behind that door.
有些日子，我确信自己能听到我的书在那扇门后尖叫。

01:03:04.969 --> 01:03:12.090
Not enough anesthesia had been administered before surgery and she'd woken up, screaming, mid incision.
手术前麻醉没打够，结果她在开刀开到一半时醒了过来，放声尖叫。

01:03:12.090 --> 01:03:19.010
I became hyper aware that 300 pages of book could not possibly fit into 110 pages of screenplay.
我高度意识到，300页的书根本不可能塞进110页的剧本里。

01:03:19.010 --> 01:03:22.340
So which limbs were being amputated?
那么，究竟是哪些四肢被截去了呢？

01:03:22.340 --> 01:03:36.969
I could see my book's blood leaking out from under Rob's office door, the flesh of my life story dropping to the indifferent floor of the Abattoir, the guiltless butcher death to its cries for mercy.
我能看到我的书的鲜血从罗布的办公室门缝下流出来，我人生故事的血肉落在了屠宰场冷漠的地板上，那个毫无负罪感的屠夫对它的求饶声充耳不闻。

01:03:36.969 --> 01:03:42.320
And then finally, the stone cold silence of death.
然后，最终迎来了死亡那般冰冷的死寂。

01:03:42.719 --> 01:03:46.760
Rob, man, it felt so great to be writing again.
罗布，老兄，重新开始写作的感觉真是太棒了。

01:03:46.760 --> 01:03:52.960
Having a deadline, a bullseye to hit, a raison d'etre, Paige was happy too, I could tell.
有了截稿日期、有了要命中的靶心、有了生存的意义，佩姬也很高兴，我看得出来。

01:03:52.960 --> 01:03:55.360
Interested in my progress, very supportive.
她对我的进展很感兴趣，也非常支持。

01:03:55.360 --> 01:04:00.079
She was relieved this had stayed in the family, rather than being outsourced to some hack she'd never met.
她很庆幸这件事留在了家里，而不是外包给某个她从未见过的文人墨客。

01:04:00.079 --> 01:04:01.840
That would have been a nightmare.
那才真是一场噩梦。

01:04:01.840 --> 01:04:08.840
Plus, if this movie came out great, with my name in the credits, career back on track.
另外，如果这部电影大获成功，演职员表里写着我的名字，我的职业生涯就能重回正轨。

01:04:08.840 --> 01:04:10.239
The script was flowing too.
剧本的进展也很顺利。

01:04:10.239 --> 01:04:11.599
It was writing itself.
简直文思泉涌。

01:04:11.599 --> 01:04:16.360
This is what I always tell younger writers, what I was trying to teach my college students.
这就是我经常对年轻作家说的话，也是我试图教导我的大学学生的话。

01:04:16.360 --> 01:04:19.433
absurdly, I still had months left of that charade.
荒谬的是，我还要在那种假象中度过几个月。

01:04:19.433 --> 01:04:21.400
Writing doesn't have to be hard.
写作其实并不难。

01:04:21.400 --> 01:04:28.851
If you're writing a script you believe in with a clear story and well-defined characters, it should feel easy.
如果你在写一个你深信不疑的剧本，有着清晰的故事和定义明确的角色，那应该感觉很简单。

01:04:28.851 --> 01:04:29.867
It should flow.
它应该顺畅地流淌出来。

01:04:29.867 --> 01:04:32.035
Right now, I was in that pocket.
此刻，我就处在那种游刃有余的状态中。

01:04:32.035 --> 01:04:36.099
And as a writer, that's about as close to heaven as it gets.
作为一名作家，这几乎就是人间天堂了。

01:04:36.099 --> 01:04:36.599
age.
佩姬。

01:04:36.599 --> 01:04:40.015
Those weeks were a living hell.
那几个星期简直是人间地狱。

01:04:40.015 --> 01:04:42.659
My stomach hurt nonstop.
我的胃痛得一刻也没停过。

01:04:42.599 --> 01:04:46.960
Okay, that was a little taste of the book, the audio book, I should say.
好了，刚才那只是这本书的一小部分试听，应该说是有声书。

01:04:46.960 --> 01:04:51.261
There are two other characters whose voices you also hear in the story.
故事中还有另外两个角色的声音。

01:04:51.261 --> 01:04:53.380
And I'm so excited about this book.
我对这本书感到无比兴奋。

01:04:53.380 --> 01:04:59.558
It comes out November 4 from HarperCollins and the book and the audio book are all available that day.
它将于11月4日由哈珀柯林斯出版，书和有声书都将在那一天上市。

01:04:59.558 --> 01:05:01.072
It means the world to me.
这对我有非凡的意义。

01:05:01.072 --> 01:05:06.100
It's my favorite thing I've written except for or Hymium, or in addition to Hymium.
这是我写过的最喜欢的东西，除了《老爸老妈浪漫史》，或者说是在《老爸老妈浪漫史》之外。

01:05:06.099 --> 01:05:13.400
And yeah, I would love it if Hymium fans and Hymium fans would give it a read and or listen.
是的，如果《老爸老妈浪漫史》的粉丝们能去读一读或者听一听，我会非常高兴。
